dhvāja, and author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 152);
epithet of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 152.

सस्य 1. सस्य, अम्, n. (for 1. शस्य, q. v.;
in Uṇādi-s. IV. 109. said to be fr. rt. सस्), a good
quality, excellence, merit.

1. सस्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of good qualities;
(अस्), m. a sort of precious stone (coloured like the
inner fruit of a cocoa-nut; perhaps an opal).
